  "final": "I changed `src/ledger.ts` and `src/service.ts`. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes. I didn't add any checks of my own, so the retry, concurrency and conflict behaviour is untested.\n\n**`Ledger.apply`**\n- Receipts are now stored per tenant and key. The key is `JSON.stringify([tenant, key])`, so different tenants can reuse the same key and no tenant/key pair can collide with another.\n- If the tenant/key already exists with the same cents, `apply` returns the original receipt and adds no entry.\n- If it exists with different cents, `apply` throws `Error('key conflict')` and adds no entry.\n- The lookup and insert happen with no `await` between them, so concurrent calls can't both debit.\n\n**`PaymentService.pay`**\n- It validates everything before touching the ledger or transport. Tenant and key must be nonempty strings, cents must be a positive integer, and attempts must be an integer from 1 to 5. Anything else throws `Error('invalid payment')`.\n- It now calls `apply` once, then retries only `transport.acknowledge`, passing the same receipt each time. Before, a retry re-ran the debit.\n- Only `Transient` errors are retried, up to `attempts` total tries. If the tries run out, the last `Transient` is thrown unchanged. Any other error, including `key conflict`, is thrown immediately without a retry.",
  "tools": [
